From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:56:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: power: apple,pmc: consumer-switched interface
 enables

A display pipe's BWR and boost interface enables are described as a power
domain between the pipe's SYS and FE power states. The J713 internal
display's power states are firmware-owned and on from boot, while the
boot loader leaves only its boost enable set, so its enables cannot be
such a domain; macOS clears them before powering the pipe down and sets
them again after powering it up.

Add apple,consumer-switched for an interface node that is not a power
domain: the display coprocessor that refers to it clears its bits before
it powers the pipe down and restores them after it powers the pipe up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Bartosz Nitka <niteria@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 1794d64beff38672c62b988fcdbda68a6e47688b)
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml  | 20 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml
index 50e4ccc091..c7896d1320 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/apple,pmc.yaml
@@ -196,12 +196,28 @@ patternProperties:
         maximum: 31
         description: Bit of the pipe in the boost interface enable word.
 
+      apple,consumer-switched:
+        type: boolean
+        description: |
+          Not a power domain. The pipe's power is firmware-owned, and the
+          display coprocessor that refers to this node (apple,pmc-interface)
+          clears the bits before it powers the pipe down and gives them back
+          the values they had after it powers the pipe up again.
+
     required:
-      - '#power-domain-cells'
-      - power-domains
       - apple,bwr-bit
       - apple,boost-bit
 
+    oneOf:
+      - required:
+          - '#power-domain-cells'
+          - power-domains
+      - required:
+          - apple,consumer-switched
+        properties:
+          '#power-domain-cells': false
+          power-domains: false
+
   '^performance-controller@[0-9a-f]+$':
     type: object
     description: The host performance controller's voter agent.
